{"type":"message","id":"7c33f0f4","parentId":"9488b8b7","timestamp":"2026-03-04T08:53:29.217Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-e0e372ff3e5c4cd5aba3e2a743f28366","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Development Report\n\n**Date:** 2026-03-04\n**Task:** 修复 ParMETIS 优化引入的段错误\n**Agent:** code-agent\n\n## Workspace\n`/home/one/projects/cgnsMeshCutter`\n\n## Summary\n\nThe segmentation fault issue reported was **already fixed** in commit `5733c3e` (fix: ParMETIS algorithm and CMake linking issues).\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\nThe original segmentation fault was caused by a **missing `openSubMeshToWrite()` call** in the `cut_parmetis()` function. This resulted in `smallMesh_[ifile]` being `nullptr` when `rwNode()` and `rwBody()` tried to use it.\n\n## Fix Applied (in previous commit)\n\n```cpp\n// In cut_parmetis(), added before processing cells:\n// open sub-mesh file for writing (CRITICAL: must be done before rwNode/rwBody)\nthis->openSubMeshToWrite(meshFilename, ifile, np);\n```\n\n## Verification Tests\n\nAll tests passed successfully:\n\n| Test | MPI Processes | Partitions | Result |\n|------|---------------|------------|--------|\n| Mesh Partitioning | 2 | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| Mesh Partitioning | 2 | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| Mesh Partitioning | 4 | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| CFD Simulation | 2 | 2 | ✅ Converged |\n| CFD Simulation | 2 | 4 | ✅ Converged |\n\n### Sample Output (CFD Simulation with np=4)\n```\n[info] Boundary: Interface_0\n[info]     faces   : 91\n[info] Boundary: Interface_3\n[info]     faces   : 89\nmomentumEquationU residual = 0.200459\nmomentumEquationV residual = 0.171373\nmomentumEquationW residual = 0.0309303\npressurecorrectionEquation residual = 0.00198977\n```\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/metisCutter.cpp` | Added missing `openSubMeshToWrite()` call |\n| `CMakeLists.txt` | Fixed library linking |\n| `src/CMakeLists.txt` | Removed cgio library linking |\n\n## Notes on `collect_interface()` Optimization\n\nThe `collect_interface()` function uses:\n- Sparse point-to-point communication pattern\n- Binary serialization for efficiency\n- Fixed 1MB receive buffer (sufficient for current mesh sizes)\n\nThe optimization is working correctly. The binary serialization includes:\n- Face hash (size_t)\n- Face node count (int)\n- Face nodes (cgsize_t array)\n\n## Status\n✅ Ready for use - Issue was already resolved in commit 5733c3e"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772614409216}}
